The attached image, Figure 2 from the *npj Vaccines* article, illustrates that Nano-11 nanoparticles are retained at the injection site and are cleared over time. Panel A displays whole-body fluorescence images of mice, showing the Nano-11 signal strongly localized at the injection site immediately after intramuscular injection, which gradually decreases in intensity over a 21-day period. Panel B, depicting excised organs on day 21, confirms the sustained presence of Nano-11 predominantly at the injection sites and in iliac lymph nodes, with minimal distribution to other internal organs. Panel C quantifies the injection site fluorescence intensity, indicating a rapid decrease by day 1, a slight increase by day 2, and a gradual decline thereafter, with only about 20% of the initial signal remaining at day 21.